@startuml review_layout_01_plan
' Review unit 01 of 05 -- see docs/review_layout.md for the series.
' State AFTER commit 7f83754 (docs +230, no code).
' Output identical to unit 00: the commit adds one markdown file.
' Render: plantuml -tsvg docs/review_layout_01_plan.puml

title Unit 01 -- the layout plan, docs only (94efaaf..7f83754)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Monospaced
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam ArrowColor #555555
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #FCFCFC
  BorderColor #777777
  DiamondBackgroundColor #F2F2F2
  DiamondBorderColor #777777
}
skinparam partition {
  BorderColor #8899AA
  FontColor #33495E
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFDF0
  BorderColor #C8C08A
}

start

partition "docs/layout_plan.md  (NEW, 230 lines)" {
  #C8E6C9:the problem: density says how many cells are occupied,
  not where. Argo and CrocoLake fill the first k levels of each
  profile; GLORYS leaves continents empty. At occupancy 0.149 on
  a 2000x500 grid the compressed array is 1.15 MB scattered and
  0.55 MB with each line filling its first k cells, and which
  format is smaller reverses;
  #C8E6C9:the design: two parameters
  layout = how data fill the cells available (scattered, padded)
  mask_fraction = which cells are available
  padded = CF's "incomplete multidimensional array"
  (not "ragged", which CF reserves for 1-D packed forms);
  #C8E6C9:consequences recorded before any code
  minimum density rises to prod(shape)/n_padded + n_padded - 1
  overlap must raise: every line filling its first k cells of one axis
  makes F1 the ratio of the densities
  the padded axis cannot be the split dimension;
}

:no code change: every case writes the same files as unit 00;

stop

legend right
  |<#C8E6C9> green |= added or changed by THIS unit |
  |<#FFCDD2> red |= removed by THIS unit |
  |<#FFE0B2> orange |= single-variable flow touched by THIS unit |
  |<#FFF9C4> yellow |= generated data or file that changed as a result |
  | plain | unchanged since unit 00 |

  <b>What to review in unit 01</b>
  * the measurements behind the motivation
  * the two-parameter design; unit 03 later drops the mask
  * the three consequences, each implemented in unit 02
  * "every variable fills its first k cells": unit 02 pads var0
    only, see the finding there
end legend

@enduml
